# Design: xcoder-dojo — UI / Page Specification (TypeScript UI + Agent)

- Task: design-st-2c7624 (stage: design, role: business-analyst)
- Upstream: `.xcoder/backlog/requirements-st-b1522d.md` (requirements, 21 ACs, 12 security constraints S-01..S-13)
- Reference (read-only input): `xcoder-ai-dojo/` (PyQt6, v0.1.4) — blueprint §3 "User experience" and §4 module map
- Target: new sibling folder `xcoder-dojo/` (greenfield; no TS scaffold exists in this workspace)
- Scope of this document: navigation flows, page/subpage specs, per-page data requirements, display modes, UI event/action contracts, component interfaces, and the UX-vs-simplicity tradeoffs taken.
- Not in this document: module/file layout, build pipeline, process supervisor internals, LLM wire format (covered by architecture/implementation stages). Where a decision would change a page contract, it is flagged inline.

---

## 1. What "components" and "interfaces" mean here

- **Component (page/subpage):** a user-visible, independently stateable surface with its own data requirements and action set. Pages are the unit of specification, not React components. Every page below has an ID (`P-xx`) and at least one TypeScript interface describing its view-model and its action surface.
- **Interface / contract:** (a) the **page model** — the exact data a page renders, with nullability and provenance; (b) the **action contract** — name, input, preconditions, side-effect class, approval requirement, and the process that enforces it; (c) the **IPC bridge** — the only channel from page to privileged work.
- **Tradeoff:** every place where a richer UX was rejected for a simpler, enforceable contract (or the reverse), with the cost stated.

Two invariants apply to every page and are not repeated per page:

1. **UI checks are UX only** [UI-01]. Every action's authorization/validation is re-enforced in the Electron main process. A page that hides a button is not a control.
2. **All model-derived and file-derived text is untrusted** [UI-02/UI-03/UI-13, PRM-01]. It renders as escaped text or sanitized Markdown; no raw HTML, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, no remote images, no script execution, and it is labelled as AI-generated or workspace-derived.

---

## 2. Navigation flow

### 2.1 Page hierarchy

```
P-00 App Shell (persistent frame — title bar, left rail, center, right dock, bottom dock, status bar)
├─ P-01 Welcome / No-Workspace            (center, replaces P-03 while no workspace)
├─ P-02 Workspace Explorer                (left dock, lazy tree + filter)
│    └─ P-02a Node Context Menu           (subpage / transient overlay)
├─ P-03 Editor Area                       (center, tabbed)
│    ├─ P-03a Text Editor Pane            (CodeMirror 6; highlighting, line numbers, gutter)
│    ├─ P-03b Markdown Preview Pane       (split beside P-03a when tab kind = markdown)
│    └─ P-03c Unopenable File State       (binary / non-UTF-8 / too large / outside root)
├─ P-04 Run Console                       (bottom dock, single-flight)
│    └─ P-04a Run Target Picker           (subpage: resolved file/project targets)
├─ P-05 Agent Panel — JARVIS              (right dock)
│    ├─ P-05a Tool Call Card              (inline list item)
│    ├─ P-05b Turn-Limit Banner           (inline terminal state)
│    └─ P-05c Model-Not-Configured State  (inline empty state)
├─ P-06 Delegation Run View               (right dock takeover from P-05)
├─ P-07 Approval Sheet                    (modal overlay; file-write | delegation-launch)
├─ P-08 Settings                          (modal page, tabbed)
│    ├─ P-08a Model & Limits
│    ├─ P-08b Data, Secrets & Audit
│    └─ P-08c Appearance
├─ P-09 Conversation History              (drawer inside P-05)
├─ P-10 Audit Log Viewer                  (modal, cursor-paginated)
└─ P-12 Error Center                      (toast stack + detail sheet)

Persistent chrome (present on all pages):
- P-11 Status Bar  (workspace path, run state, agent state, audit-log location link, model state)
```

### 2.2 Transitions

| From | Trigger | To | Guard / failure |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P-01 | `workspace.open` (dialog or drop a folder) | P-00 + P-02 populated | Outside-root or unreadable folder → P-12 error, stay on P-01 |
| P-01 | `workspace.open` refused (path is a file) | P-12 | Explicit "select a folder" message |
| P-02 | `file.open` (double-click / Enter on file) | P-03 new tab | Unopenable → P-03c tab with error state; never a blank editor |
| P-02 | Right-click a node | P-02a | — |
| P-03 | Ctrl+S / `file.save` | P-03 (dirty cleared) | Write failure → P-12 error + tab stays dirty |
| P-03 | Tab kind = markdown | P-03b opens in split | Remote images/HTML blocked inline in preview |
| P-03 | Ctrl+R / `run.start` | P-04 | Console busy → P-04 report, no second process |
| P-04 | `run.start` with no resolvable target | P-04a | No target → explicit "no run target" error, not a silent no-op |
| P-05 | user sends a message | P-05 streaming answer + P-05a cards | No model configured → P-05c; app stays usable |
| P-05a | model emits a delegation tool call | P-07 (`delegation-launch`) | Denied → card shows `denied`, delegation never starts |
| P-07 approved (delegation) | — | P-06 | CLI missing → P-06 `failed-cli-missing` + remediation |
| P-07 approved (file-write) | — | back to originating page | Target file changed since approval → approval expires, re-prompt |
| P-05 | `session.clear` | P-05 empty transcript | — |
| P-11 | click audit-log location | P-10 | Log missing → P-12 with path shown |
| Any | unrecoverable main-process error | P-12 | Never a blank white renderer; shell renders the error page |

Navigation rules: one workspace at a time (per window); one active run at a time; one active agent request at a time; opening a second workspace requires closing the current one (unsaved-tab prompt first). This mirrors the reference's single-flight console and per-workspace agent busy state.

---

## 3. Shared contracts (referenced by every page)

```ts
// src/shared/contracts/ids.ts
export type PageId =
  | 'shell' | 'welcome' | 'explorer' | 'editor' | 'preview' | 'console'
  | 'agent' | 'delegation' | 'approval' | 'settings' | 'history' | 'audit' | 'status';
export type SupportedLanguage =
  | 'typescript' | 'javascript' | 'json' | 'markdown' | 'python' | 'html'
  | 'css' | 'shell' | 'powershell' | 'yaml' | 'sql' | 'plaintext';

// src/shared/contracts/errors.ts — the ONLY error shape a page renders.
export interface AppError {
  code: AppErrorCode;          // enumerated, never a raw stack or provider string
  message: string;             // user-facing, pre-redacted in main
  remediation?: string;        // e.g. "Install Node.js, or pick another run target"
  detailRef?: string;          // opaque id -> full detail in P-10, not in the toast
}
export type AppErrorCode =
  | 'workspace-not-open' | 'path-escape' | 'credential-file' | 'excluded-dir'
  | 'binary-file' | 'not-utf8' | 'file-too-large' | 'write-failed' | 'run-busy'
  | 'run-spawn-failed' | 'runtime-missing' | 'model-not-configured' | 'model-error'
  | 'schema-invalid' | 'tool-not-allowlisted' | 'turn-limit' | 'request-cap-reached'
  | 'delegation-cli-missing' | 'workspace-changed' | 'approval-expired'
  | 'secret-detected' | 'unknown';

// src/shared/contracts/action.ts — the action contract shared by pages and main.
export type SideEffect = 'none' | 'read' | 'write' | 'execute' | 'secret';
export interface ActionDescriptor<In, Out> {
  readonly name: ActionName;
  readonly page: PageId;
  readonly sideEffect: SideEffect;
  readonly requiresApproval: boolean; // true => P-07 must interpose
  readonly enforcedIn: 'main';        // never 'renderer' — see [UI-01]
  validate(input: unknown): In;       // throws AppError('schema-invalid')
  run(input: In): Promise<Out>;
}
export type ActionName =
  | 'workspace.open' | 'workspace.close'
  | 'tree.listChildren' | 'tree.revealPath' | 'tree.filter'
  | 'file.open' | 'file.save' | 'file.saveAll' | 'file.close' | 'file.revert'
  | 'run.resolveTargets' | 'run.start' | 'run.stop' | 'run.clearConsole'
  | 'agent.send' | 'agent.stop' | 'agent.retryLast'
  | 'session.list' | 'session.load' | 'session.clear'
  | 'delegation.launch' | 'delegation.stop'
  | 'approval.list' | 'approval.respond'
  | 'settings.get' | 'settings.update' | 'settings.setApiKey' | 'settings.clearApiKey'
  | 'audit.page' | 'audit.location';
```

```ts
// src/shared/contracts/bridge.ts — the whole privileged surface. Nothing else is exposed.
export interface DojoBridge {
  workspace: {
    openDialog(): Promise<WorkspaceOpened>;              // user gesture in main; renderer never supplies a raw path
    openPath(relOrAbs: string): Promise<WorkspaceOpened>; // validated in main, resolved + root-confined
    close(): Promise<void>;
    current(): Promise<WorkspaceOpened | null>;
  };
  tree: {
    listChildren(request: ListChildrenRequest): Promise<TreeNodePage>;
  };
  files: {
    read(relPath: string): Promise<FileReadResult>;      // result carries encoding/eol/kind or an AppError
    save(request: SaveRequest): Promise<SaveResult>;      // requires approval if agent-initiated
  };
  run: {
    resolveTargets(relPath: string): Promise<RunTarget[]>;
    start(request: RunStartRequest): Promise<RunSession>;
    stop(runId: string): Promise<RunSession>;
    onEvent(handler: (event: RunEvent) => void): Unsubscribe;
  };
  agent: {
    send(request: AgentSendRequest): Promise<{ requestId: string }>;
    stop(requestId: string): Promise<void>;
    onEvent(handler: (event: AgentEvent) => void): Unsubscribe;
  };
  session: {
    list(): Promise<SessionSummary[]>;
    load(sessionId: string): Promise<SessionDetail>;
    clear(sessionId: string): Promise<void>;
  };
  delegation: {
    launch(request: DelegationLaunchRequest): Promise<DelegationRun>;
    stop(delegationId: string): Promise<DelegationRun>;
    onEvent(handler: (event: DelegationEvent) => void): Unsubscribe;
  };
  approval: {
    list(): Promise<ApprovalRequest[]>;
    respond(decision: { approvalId: string; decision: ApprovalDecision }): Promise<ApprovalRequest>;
    onRequest(handler: (request: ApprovalRequest) => void): Unsubscribe;
  };
  settings: {
    get(): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;
    update(patch: LlmSettingsPatch): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;
    setApiKey(input: ApiKeyInput): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;  // write-only; never echoed back
    clearApiKey(): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;
  };
  audit: {
    page(request: AuditPageRequest): Promise<AuditPage>;
    location(): Promise<{ logDir: string; retentionDays: number }>;
  };
  errors: {
    onError(handler: (error: AppError) => void): Unsubscribe;
  };
}
export type Unsubscribe = () => void;
```

Bridge rules (enforced in `preload`, not by convention): no `ipcRenderer` exposure; channels are an explicit allowlist; every payload is schema-validated in main before use; every response is a discriminated `{ ok: true, value } | { ok: false, error: AppError }`; the API key is **never** returnable — only `hasApiKey: boolean` [UI-07, S-02, AI-06].

---

## 4. P-00 App Shell

**Purpose:** the persistent frame that makes workspace and command context explicit (a stated product principle). It is not a route; it owns layout and chrome.

**Regions:** title bar (app name `Xcoder Dojo`, active workspace absolute path, dirty-tab count) · left dock (P-02) · center (P-01 or P-03) · right dock (P-05 or P-06) · bottom dock (P-04) · status bar (P-11) · overlay slot (P-07, P-08, P-10, P-12).

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| appVersion | main (`app.getVersion`) | string | shown in P-08c |
| workspaceId | `workspace.current` | string \| null | null → P-01 |
| workspacePathDisplay | main, path-normalized | string \| null | absolute, always visible |
| openTabCount / dirtyCount | editor store | number | drives close/save prompt |
| rightDockMode | UI state | `'agent' \| 'delegation' \| 'collapsed'` | — |
| bottomDockMode | UI state | `'console' \| 'collapsed'` | — |
| dockSizes | persisted UI state | `Record<DockId, number>` | restored on start |
| modelState | `settings.get` | `'configured' \| 'missing' \| 'error'` | surface in P-11 |

**Interface**

```ts
export interface ShellModel {
  appVersion: string;
  workspace: { workspaceId: string; pathDisplay: string; name: string } | null;
  openTabCount: number;
  dirtyCount: number;
  rightDock: { mode: 'agent' | 'delegation' | 'collapsed'; width: number };
  bottomDock: { mode: 'console' | 'collapsed'; height: number };
  modelState: 'configured' | 'missing' | 'error';
}
export interface ShellActions {
  openWorkspace(): Promise<void>;      // -> workspace.open
  closeWorkspace(): Promise<void>;     // -> workspace.close (unsaved prompt first)
  toggleDock(dock: 'right' | 'bottom'): void;
  focusEditor(): void;
  openSettings(): void;
  openAuditLog(): void;
}
```

**Display modes:** view (chrome), no list/detail. **States:** loading (skeleton docks, workspace resolving), ready, degraded (model missing → banner, not a modal), fatal (renderer failed → P-12 shell error page).

---

## 5. P-01 Welcome / No-Workspace

**Purpose:** the only page reachable with `workspaceId === null`. Must never look like a broken editor.

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type |
| --- | --- | --- |
| recentWorkspaces | main store (paths only, no file contents) | `RecentWorkspace[]` (max 10, `{ pathDisplay, lastOpenedAtMs }`) |
| modelState + provider/model label | `settings.get` | `LlmSettingsView` |
| startableHint | derived | string ("Open a folder to begin") |

**Interface**

```ts
export interface WelcomeModel {
  recentWorkspaces: ReadonlyArray<{ pathDisplay: string; lastOpenedAtMs: number }>;
  modelState: 'configured' | 'missing' | 'error';
  modelLabel: string | null;   // e.g. "gpt-x @ openai-compatible" — never a key or full URL with creds
}
export interface WelcomeActions {
  chooseFolder(): Promise<void>;                 // -> workspace.open (OS dialog only)
  openRecent(pathDisplay: string): Promise<void>; // main re-validates; stale entry -> P-12 + remove from list
  openSettings(): void;
}
```

**Display modes:** list (recent, sortable by recency, max 10, not paginated), view. **Empty state:** no recents → the choose-folder CTA with a one-line explanation. **Guards:** no path is ever typed by the user into this page (a free-text path field would create an unvalidated path input surface).

---

## 6. P-02 Workspace Explorer

**Purpose:** lazy file tree confined to the opened workspace root; the discovery surface for every file action.

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| children of a dir | `tree.listChildren` | `FileNode[]` | one directory per call; never a whole-tree walk |
| relPath | main | string | POSIX separators, always root-relative |
| kind | main | `'file' \| 'dir'` | — |
| hasChildren | main | boolean | drives the expand chevron without a second call |
| language | main (extension map) | `SupportedLanguage` | drives the language chip, not the save path |
| sizeBytes / mtimeMs | main stat | number | sortable columns |
| truncated / scannedFiles | main | boolean / number | exposes the 1500-file scan bound honestly |
| excludedReason | main | `'hidden' \| 'generated' \| 'credential' \| null` | excluded nodes are **not listed**; the reason is used only in refusal messages |

```ts
export interface FileNode {
  nodeId: string;            // stable: hash of relPath
  relPath: string;
  name: string;
  kind: 'file' | 'dir';
  hasChildren: boolean;
  language?: SupportedLanguage;
  sizeBytes?: number;
  mtimeMs?: number;
}
export interface ListChildrenRequest { parentRelPath: string | null; cursor?: string; limit?: number; }
export interface TreeNodePage {
  parentRelPath: string | null;
  entries: FileNode[];
  nextCursor: string | null;   // null => no more
  truncated: boolean;          // true => hit file/scan bound
  scannedFiles: number;        // vs. configured 1500 cap
}
export interface ExplorerModel {
  workspaceRootLabel: string;
  expandedRelPaths: ReadonlyArray<string>;
  nodesByParent: Readonly<Record<string, TreeNodePage>>;
  selection: { relPath: string; kind: 'file' | 'dir' } | null;
  filter: { text: string; applied: boolean };   // filters loaded children only — see T-05
  loadingParents: ReadonlyArray<string>;
}
export interface ExplorerActions {
  expand(relPath: string): Promise<void>;              // tree.listChildren
  collapse(relPath: string): void;
  refresh(relPath: string): Promise<void>;
  openFile(relPath: string): Promise<void>;            // file.open -> P-03
  revealInExplorer(relPath: string): Promise<void>;    // OS reveal; workspace-confined
  copyRelativePath(relPath: string): Promise<void>;    // clipboard only, never a secret path
  filter(text: string): void;
}
```

**Display modes:** list (hierarchical, virtualized), sortable (name, size, mtime — client-side on loaded nodes), searchable (filter on loaded nodes), paginated/lazy (per-directory `nextCursor`). **States:** loading (per-node spinner, tree stays interactive), empty dir, truncated dir (inline "showing first N of M" with the bound named), error (per-node retry, not a whole-tree failure), workspace-changed (stale nodes → banner + refresh action).
**Security:** absolute paths, `..`, dotfiles, generated dirs and credential-shaped names never appear and any attempt to request them returns `AppError('path-escape' | 'credential-file' | 'excluded-dir')` from main [S-06]. The tree is a projection of a server-side decision, not a client-side filter.

---

## 7. P-03 Editor Area (with P-03a / P-03b / P-03c)

**Purpose:** tabbed editing with highlighting, line numbers, encoding/EOL fidelity, and a Markdown split preview.

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| tabs | renderer store, hydrated from `files.read` | `EditorTabState[]` | order = open order, MRU on re-open |
| encoding | main (BOM sniff) | `'utf-8' \| 'utf-8-bom'` | preserved on save, never silently normalized |
| eol | main (first-line detect) | `'lf' \| 'crlf'` | preserved on save |
| dirty | renderer (buffer vs. saved sha) | boolean | drives close prompt + tab dot |
| language | main | `SupportedLanguage` | CodeMirror mode |
| content | `files.read` | string | capped; `truncated` flag when the read bound applies |
| errorCode | main | `FileOpenErrorCode` | P-03c only |
| savedAtMs / savedSha | main | number / string | optimistic-concurrency token for save |

```ts
export type FileOpenErrorCode =
  | 'binary-file' | 'not-utf8' | 'file-too-large' | 'outside-workspace' | 'denied-credential' | 'missing';
export interface EditorTabState {
  tabId: string;
  relPath: string;
  kind: 'text' | 'markdown' | 'error';
  language: SupportedLanguage;
  encoding: 'utf-8' | 'utf-8-bom';
  eol: 'lf' | 'crlf';
  dirty: boolean;
  readOnly: boolean;
  truncated: boolean;
  errorCode?: FileOpenErrorCode;
  savedSha: string | null;
}
export interface FileReadResult {
  relPath: string; content: string; encoding: 'utf-8' | 'utf-8-bom'; eol: 'lf' | 'crlf';
  language: SupportedLanguage; sizeBytes: number; truncated: boolean; savedSha: string;
}
export interface SaveRequest { tabId: string; relPath: string; content: string; baseSha: string; writeNewFile: boolean; }
export interface SaveResult { ok: boolean; relPath: string; bytesWritten: number; encoding: 'utf-8' | 'utf-8-bom'; eol: 'lf' | 'crlf'; savedSha: string; savedAtMs: number; error?: AppError; }
export interface EditorModel {
  tabs: ReadonlyArray<EditorTabState>;
  activeTabId: string | null;
  splitPreview: { open: boolean; tabId: string | null };
  saveInFlight: ReadonlyArray<string>;   // tabIds
}
export interface EditorActions {
  open(relPath: string): Promise<void>;         // file.open
  activate(tabId: string): void;
  close(tabId: string): Promise<void>;          // dirty -> save/discard prompt
  save(tabId: string): Promise<SaveResult>;     // file.save
  saveAll(): Promise<ReadonlyArray<SaveResult>>;
  revert(tabId: string): Promise<void>;         // file.revert (discards buffer)
  togglePreview(tabId: string): void;           // markdown only
  find(text: string): void;                     // CodeMirror search, no IPC
}
```

**Display modes:** editable (content), view (tab strip, gutter), detail (per-tab metadata in the status strip: language, encoding, EOL, dirty). No pagination — one buffer is loaded whole, or the tab is P-03c.

**P-03a Text Editor Pane:** CodeMirror 6; syntax highlighting + line numbers for the `language` set; find/replace in-editor; no remote resource loading; no HTML rendering of file content (always text).
**P-03b Markdown Preview Pane:** debounced render of sanitized Markdown; **local images only** resolved through a root-confined file URL; embedded raw HTML and remote images are skipped and the skip is annotated inline (a "1 remote image blocked" note) so the omission is visible, not silent.
**P-03c Unopenable File State:** renders the specific `errorCode` with remediation ("This file is not UTF-8 text. It was not opened, and nothing was modified."), keeps the tab closable, and never shows a partial/garbled buffer [AC-05].
**States:** clean, dirty, saving (input stays live, save is idempotent by `baseSha`), conflict (`baseSha` mismatch → "file changed on disk", offer reload/diff/overwrite-with-approval), read-only (outside write permission or newly denied path).
**Security:** file content is rendered as text, never HTML [UI-02/UI-03]; save is `sideEffect: 'write'` and passes through P-07 when the write was agent-initiated [S-07]; no path may resolve outside root.

---

## 8. P-04 Run Console (with P-04a Run Target Picker)

**Purpose:** the single execution surface — resolve a runnable target, execute it, stream stdout/stderr, show the exit code, and let the user stop it.

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| resolved targets | `run.resolveTargets` | `RunTarget[]` | file kind, package script, or project manifest — mirrors the reference runtime matrix |
| argv | main | `string[]` | **argv array, never a shell string** [S-08, PRM-08] |
| cwdRelPath | main | string | always inside the workspace |
| state | main events | `RunState` | `idle→starting→running→stopping→exited \| failed` |
| chunks | `run.onEvent` | `ConsoleChunk[]` | ring buffer with per-run cap |
| exitCode / signal | main | `number \| null` / `string?` | surfaced explicitly, including non-zero [AC-06/AC-08] |
| truncated | main | `{stdout,stderr}` | reports when the output cap was hit [AC-19] |

```ts
export type RunState = 'idle' | 'starting' | 'running' | 'stopping' | 'exited' | 'failed';
export interface CommandSpec { argv: ReadonlyArray<string>; cwdRelPath: string; envKeys: ReadonlyArray<string>; }
export interface RunTarget {
  targetId: string; label: string; kind: 'file' | 'script' | 'project';
  relPath: string; command: CommandSpec;
  source: 'file-extension' | 'package-script' | 'project-manifest' | 'user-override';
  requiresRuntime: string | null;   // "node" | "python" | "pwsh" — surfaced before start
}
export interface ConsoleChunk { runId: string; seq: number; stream: 'stdout' | 'stderr' | 'system'; text: string; atMs: number; }
export interface RunSession {
  runId: string; targetId: string; state: RunState; startedAtMs: number;
  exitCode: number | null; signal?: string; truncated: { stdout: boolean; stderr: boolean };
}
export interface ConsoleModel {
  session: RunSession | null;
  chunks: ReadonlyArray<ConsoleChunk>;   // capped, oldest dropped first
  targets: ReadonlyArray<RunTarget>;
  selectedTargetId: string | null;
  pendingTargetFor: string | null;       // relPath awaiting picker choice
}
export interface ConsoleActions {
  resolveTargets(relPath: string): Promise<ReadonlyArray<RunTarget>>;  // run.resolveTargets
  start(targetId: string): Promise<RunSession>;                        // run.start
  stop(): Promise<RunSession>;                                        // run.stop
  clearConsole(): void;                                               // run.clearConsole (client-side)
  copyOutput(): Promise<void>;                                        // redacted text only
}
```

**Display modes:** view + append-only stream; list (chunks, virtualized, filterable by stream via the stderr/stdout toggle); sortable N/A (time-ordered, immutable); searchable (in-console find over buffered text); paginated (ring-buffer windowing, not server paging).
**States:** idle, starting, running, stopping (Stop acknowledged, awaiting exit), exited-with-0, exited-non-zero (explicit bar: "exit code 1"), failed-to-spawn (`runtime-missing` → remediation naming the runtime), busy (`run-busy` when a run is active — single-flight, no queue), truncated output (explicit note).
**Security:** no shell interpolation; Stop is a real terminate with a timeout escalation; env is an allowlist of keys, not the full parent environment; copy-output passes through the redactor [S-08, S-11].
**AC coverage:** AC-06 (streams stdout+stderr, exit code), AC-07 (single-flight + Stop reported), AC-08 (missing runtime / non-zero exit explicit), AC-19 (cap + reported truncation).

