## 9. P-05 Agent Panel (JARVIS)

**Purpose:** the conversational surface — user asks, the agent inspects the workspace through allowlisted tools, and answers stream with visible tool-call cards.

**Data requirements**

| Field | Source | Type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| transcript | `session.load` + `agent.onEvent` | `TranscriptEntry[]` | survives restart [AC-17] |
| modelState | `settings.get` | `'configured' \| 'missing' \| 'error'` | missing → P-05c, rest of app usable [AC-16] |
| requestState | agent events | `AgentRequestState` | drives Stop + send affordance |
| toolCalls | agent events | `ToolCallRecord[]` | each with args summary, duration, outcome |
| turnCount / turnCap | agent events | number | drives P-05b |
| streamed text | `agent.onEvent` | append-only | labelled AI-generated [UI-13] |
| requestCapRemaining | agent events | number | cost control surface [S-10] |

```ts
export type AgentRequestState =
  | 'idle' | 'thinking' | 'awaiting-tool' | 'answering' | 'stopping'
  | 'done' | 'stopped' | 'turn-limit' | 'request-cap' | 'failed';

export type ToolCallOutcome =
  | 'pending' | 'ok' | 'refused-sandbox' | 'refused-credential' | 'refused-excluded'
  | 'denied-allowlist' | 'denied-approval' | 'schema-invalid' | 'error';

export interface ToolCallRecord {                    // P-05a
  toolCallId: string;
  toolName: AllowlistedToolName;                     // union of the 11 allowlisted tools
  argsSummary: Readonly<Record<string, string | number | boolean>>; // display-only, redacted
  argsRedacted: boolean;
  outcome: ToolCallOutcome;
  durationMs: number | null;
  resultSummary: string | null;                      // one-line, escaped, never full file content
  resultTruncated: boolean;
}

export type AllowlistedToolName =
  | 'list_dir' | 'glob' | 'grep' | 'read_file' | 'read_multiple_files'
  | 'read_file_lines' | 'read_outline' | 'validate_file'
  | 'git_status' | 'git_diff' | 'git_log';

export interface TranscriptEntry {
  entryId: string;
  role: 'user' | 'assistant' | 'system';
  origin: 'human' | 'model' | 'workspace-data';   // renderer labels model + workspace data
  text: string;                                   // rendered escaped; markdown sanitized
  atMs: number;
  streaming: boolean;
  toolCallIds: ReadonlyArray<string>;
  rejectionNotice?: { code: AppErrorCode; message: string };  // fabricated tool name etc.
}

export interface AgentSendRequest {
  text: string;               // length-limited in main before it reaches a model [S-10]
  sessionId: string;
  workspaceId: string;
}

export type AgentEvent =
  | { type: 'request-started'; requestId: string }
  | { type: 'delta'; requestId: string; entryId: string; text: string }
  | { type: 'tool-call'; requestId: string; record: ToolCallRecord }
  | { type: 'tool-call-updated'; requestId: string; record: ToolCallRecord }
  | { type: 'entry-completed'; requestId: string; entryId: string }
  | { type: 'request-ended'; requestId: string; state: AgentRequestState; reason?: AppError }
  | { type: 'turn-progress'; requestId: string; turnCount: number; turnCap: number };

export interface AgentModel {
  sessionId: string;
  transcript: ReadonlyArray<TranscriptEntry>;
  toolCallsById: Readonly<Record<string, ToolCallRecord>>;
  request: { requestId: string | null; state: AgentRequestState; turnCount: number; turnCap: number };
  modelState: 'configured' | 'missing' | 'error';
  input: { draftText: string; maxChars: number };   // maxChars disclosed, not silent
  requestCapRemaining: number;
}
export interface AgentActions {
  send(text: string): Promise<{ requestId: string }>;  // agent.send
  stop(): Promise<void>;                               // agent.stop — aborts in-flight [S-10 kill switch]
  retryLast(): Promise<{ requestId: string }>;         // agent.retryLast
  clearConversation(): Promise<void>;                  // session.clear
  openHistory(): void;                                 // P-09
  copyEntry(entryId: string): Promise<void>;           // redacted text
}
```

**Display modes:** view + append-only transcript (immutable once complete); list (tool-call cards, collapsible, filterable by outcome); searchable (find within loaded transcript); paginated (transcript lazy-loads older entries from the session store — `session.load` pages). No editable history: the transcript is an audit-visible record, not a scratchpad — see T-09.

**P-05a Tool Call Card:** one row per call: tool name, redacted args, outcome chip, duration, one-line result summary + truncation marker. Refusals render as first-class outcomes (`refused-sandbox`, `denied-allowlist`) so the user sees the boundary working rather than a generic failure [AC-11, AC-12].
**P-05b Turn-Limit Banner:** terminal state with `turnCount/turnCap` and an explicit "stopped at turn limit" label — never presented as an answer [AC-10].
**P-05c Model-Not-Configured State:** inline empty state with a settings CTA; sending is disabled but editor/tree/console stay fully usable [AC-16].
**States:** idle, thinking, awaiting-tool, answering (streaming), stopping, done, stopped, turn-limit, request-cap, failed, schema-rejected (inline rejection notice on the offending turn).
**Security:** every tool result and file excerpt injected into context is rendered and persisted as `origin:'workspace-data'` and delimited as untrusted; assistant text is labelled AI-generated; a tool name outside `AllowlistedToolName` is refused with `tool-not-allowlisted` and never dispatched [S-03/04, PRM-04/07/08]; the full prompt/log path is never rendered here [PRM-03].
**AC coverage:** AC-09, AC-10, AC-12, AC-16, AC-17, AC-19.

